  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A chunky rope plant hanger holds a large 15, 20 cm pot in a thick open-mesh cup worked from a "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "magic ring",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "magic-ring"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Super-chunky cotton rope or T-shirt yarn works on a 10 mm hook. The whole hanger takes under two hours to complete. The thick cords hold heavy pots without strain, and the open cup lets the terracotta breathe."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "slug": "crochet-hook",
              "label": "10 mm crochet hook",
              "isOptional": false
            },
            {
              "slug": "tapestry-needle",
              "label": "Tapestry needle (large eye)",
              "isOptional": false
            },
            {
              "slug": "craft-scissors",
              "label": "Scissors",
              "isOptional": false
            },
            {
              "slug": "stitch-marker",
              "label": "Stitch marker",
              "isOptional": false
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Materials"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "60 m super-chunky cotton rope or T-shirt yarn (3 mm rope diameter works well). One ball of 100 m is enough for two hangers."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "1 wooden ring, 4 cm diameter, for the hanging loop, or use a sturdy metal ring."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gauge"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "7 dc × 9 rows = 10 × 10 cm in super-chunky cotton rope with a 10 mm hook, unblocked. Gauge is approximate: adjust cup size by adding or removing rounds."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Stitches used"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "bulletList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Magic ring (MR)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Chain (ch)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Slip stitch (sl st)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Double crochet (dc). UK term; US equivalent is single crochet (sc)"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pattern"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cup (worked flat, in the round)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "MR: ch 3, 11 tr into the ring, sl st to top of ch 3 to join (12 sts)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 2: ch 1, 2 dc in each st around, sl st to join (24 sts)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Round 3: ch 1, *1 dc in next st, 2 dc in next st; repeat from * around, sl st to join (36 sts)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Rounds 4, 5: ch 1, 1 dc in each st, sl st to join (36 sts). This builds the cup sides."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hanging cords (work 4, one at each quarter-point)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mark 4 evenly-spaced points on the cup rim (stitch 1, 10, 19, 28 on the 36-st round)."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Attach yarn at a marker. Ch 60 (approx. 45 cm). Sl st back along the chain to the cup rim to form a thick cord. Fasten off leaving a 30 cm tail."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Repeat for the other 3 marked points."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gather"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Thread all 4 cord tails through the wooden ring. Pull even and knot securely. Trim tails to 3 cm and weave in with the tapestry needle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in all ends. The thick cotton rope does not need blocking: it holds its shape under the weight of the pot."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Care"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Handwash or machine-wash on a 30°C gentle cycle. Hang to dry with the pot removed. Cotton rope yellows slightly with age in direct sun: position away from a south-facing window if colour-retention matters."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}